+
+dnl The release tarball does not ship libgcrypt's AM_PATH_LIBGCRYPT macro.
+dnl Crypto is disabled in this router candidate, but an unexpanded invocation
+dnl still makes the generated configure script invalid shell.  When the macro
+dnl is unavailable, expand its caller-supplied failure branch.  An explicit
+dnl --enable-crypto therefore still fails closed instead of silently building.
+m4_ifndef([AM_PATH_LIBGCRYPT], [
+AC_DEFUN([AM_PATH_LIBGCRYPT], [$3])
+])
 
